      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe worth adding a separate flag `pkvm_ramoops_console_present` (similarly to the `pvmfw_present`), so that we can check it instead of this verbose `if (pkvm_ramoops_console_pa \u0026\u0026 pkvm_ramoops_console_size)` in every place where we need to check if ramoops is available?\n\nOr we could just check if `pkvm_ramoops_console_size` is non-zero, without checking `pkvm_ramoops_console_pa`, like pKVM-ARM just checks `pvmfw_size`. (I don\u0027t really remember why exactly I decided to introduce that `pvmfw_present` back in the day, instead of doing what pKVM-ARM does.)\n\nAre there any reasons why we need to forbid using ramoops at address 0?",
      "revId": "e0a8d34742ed0770c343310eb24a5229eb92e45b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
