      "writtenOn": "2026-04-20T19:13:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think introducing yet another global variable is not best practice. However checking only pkvm_ramoops_console_size should be enough here (and next patches).\n\n\u003e Are there any reasons why we need to forbid using ramoops at address 0?\n\nI think we should forbid ramoops at address 0 because there is BIOS-related stuff reserved at the bottom of memory on x86 (see https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c#L808)\nBut since we already setting pkvm_ramoops_console_size only if the pkvm_ramoops_console_pa is not 0 (see previous commit) doing validation based on size not equal to 0 should be sufficient.",
      "parentUuid": "7290a9ca_2a23d3a8",
